    },
    {
      "type": "edit",
      "id": "3e2c565c329377a1",
      "item": {
        "type": "pagefold",
        "id": "3e2c565c329377a1",
        "text": "where am I stuck on this page?"
      },
      "date": 1748887487027
    },
    {
      "item": {
        "type": "factory",
        "id": "8aaf9d03a49d5721"
      },
      "id": "8aaf9d03a49d5721",
      "type": "add",
      "after": "3e2c565c329377a1",
      "date": 1748887488910
    },
    {
      "type": "edit",
      "id": "8aaf9d03a49d5721",
      "item": {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "id": "8aaf9d03a49d5721",
        "text": "Two tangles. wiki-ssg publishes sitemap.xml with localhost domain names. It does not know the local and public domain names and does not replace the content."
      },
      "date": 1748887594591
    },
    {
      "type": "add",
      "id": "3116dd7be51f2ad8",
      "item": {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "id": "3116dd7be51f2ad8",
        "text": "I have some ways to find and replace those name. Probably only saved in my shell history as simple perl one-liners or short scripts."
      },
      "after": "8aaf9d03a49d5721",
      "date": 1748887663908
    },
    {
      "type": "add",
      "id": "38675d91fa0e339c",
      "item": {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "id": "38675d91fa0e339c",
        "text": "There are edge cases. What if, in somewhat hasty editing, I create references on pages in deploy.localhost to dev.localhost or config.localhost. The publication workflow needs some linting or auditing tools to notice these."
      },
      "after": "3116dd7be51f2ad8",
      "date": 1748887782869
    },
    {
      "type": "add",
      "id": "3ef4327a1f2f242e",
      "item": {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "id": "3ef4327a1f2f242e",
        "text": "I don't have a clear mental model of how I upgrade the wiki client code with wiki-ssg."
      },
      "after": "38675d91fa0e339c",
      "date": 1748887811908
    },
    {
      "type": "edit",
      "id": "38675d91fa0e339c",
      "item": {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "id": "38675d91fa0e339c",
        "text": "There are edge cases. What if, in somewhat hasty editing, I create references on pages in deploy.localhost to dev.localhost or config.localhost. The publication workflow needs some linting or auditing tools to notice other localhost names that won't work in public. This imposes some cognitive load on my editorial brain to think about the constellation of local wikis and which ones are published and how are they cross-linked."
      },
      "date": 1748887904900
    },
    {
      "type": "add",
      "id": "14c5df9955092142",
      "item": {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "id": "14c5df9955092142",
        "text": "All of the above, but for forked pages and frame scripts and images."
      },
      "after": "38675d91fa0e339c",
      "date": 1748887934633
    },
    {
      "type": "add",
      "id": "a81371c7527024a3",
      "item": {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "id": "a81371c7527024a3",
        "text": "Hard to let myself document the publishing workflow because I am distracted by some known bugs I haven't decided how to fix."
      },
      "after": "3e2c565c329377a1",
      "date": 1748887998146
    },
